Source: kvlite
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: KVLite packagers <webong@users.noreply.github.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), golang-go (>= 1.23), ca-certificates
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/webong/KVlite
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: kvlite
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: KVLite pluggable key-value host CLI (no default engine)
 The driverless host: core plus the ephemeral memory engine, discovering
 every installed driver and launching verified protocol executables.
 Install a driver package for persistence.
 .
 Set KVLITE_SYSTEM_MODULE_PATH=/usr/lib/kvlite (installed by default in
 /etc/profile.d/kvlite.sh) and run `kvlite serve` or `kvlite module list`.

Package: kvlite-leveldb
Architecture: any
Depends: kvlite, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: KVLite LevelDB storage driver bundle (pure Go)
 The LevelDB engine as a versioned, checksummed module catalog. No engine
 choice is made for you beyond this package: install it for persistence,
 or serve memory straight from the host package.

Package: kvlite-badgerdb
Architecture: any
Depends: kvlite, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: KVLite BadgerDB storage driver bundle (pure Go)
 The BadgerDB engine as a versioned, checksummed module catalog. No engine
 choice is made for you beyond this package: install it for persistence,
 or serve memory straight from the host package.

Package: kvlite-boltdb
Architecture: any
Depends: kvlite, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: KVLite BoltDB storage driver bundle (pure Go, bbolt)
 The BoltDB-compatible engine, backed by the maintained bbolt fork, as a
 versioned, checksummed module catalog. No engine choice is made for you
 beyond this package.

Package: kvlite-lmdb
Architecture: any
Depends: kvlite, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: KVLite LMDB storage driver bundle (bundled LMDB C source)
 The LMDB engine as a versioned, checksummed module catalog. Needs no system
 LMDB library: the pinned binding compiles the bundled LMDB 0.9 C source,
 and the package ships both the lmdb-go and bundled OpenLDAP notices.

Package: kvlite-http
Architecture: any
Depends: kvlite, kvlite-leveldb | kvlite-badgerdb | kvlite-boltdb | kvlite-lmdb | kvlite-rocksdb, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: KVLite standalone JSON/HTTP protocol module
 The kvlite-http executable module: a direct owner or an HTTP owner for
 attached Redis processes. Needs the host plus one driver package.

Package: kvlite-redis
Architecture: any
Depends: kvlite, kvlite-leveldb | kvlite-badgerdb | kvlite-boltdb | kvlite-lmdb | kvlite-rocksdb, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: KVLite standalone Redis-compatible protocol module
 The kvlite-redis executable module: a direct owner or an attached process
 over an HTTP owner. Needs the host plus one driver package.

# RocksDB is intentionally not built by default: it needs a native toolchain
# and the distro library name moves with every SONAME bump. To add it, give
# this package a name that exists on your target release, e.g.
#   apt-cache policy 'librocksdb*'
# then uncomment the stanza, set the dependency, and add "rocksdb" to
# DRIVER_PACKAGES in debian/rules. The bundle links the system engine
# dynamically and verifies it at install time (install.sh --no-cli-link, so
# bin/kvlite stays single-owned); prefer a --bundle-runtime build wherever
# the system library cannot be pinned (see packaging/README.md).
#
# Package: kvlite-rocksdb
# Architecture: any
# Depends: kvlite, librocksdbX, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
# Description: KVLite RocksDB storage driver (system engine)
#  The RocksDB driver bundle for KVLite, composed with the distro engine:
#  no engine code ships in this package. Any installed kvlite host drives
#  it (install.sh --no-cli-link keeps bin/kvlite single-owned).
